1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,570
(All people, organizations, businesses,
events, and places shown are fictional.)

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,005
(Child actors filmed in a safe space
with their guardians present.)

3
00:00:05,973 --> 00:00:07,107
Can't you just…

4
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:10,611
stay by my side?

5
00:00:11,561 --> 00:00:12,555
What?

6
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,628
What do you mean,
"stay by your side?"

7
00:00:16,617 --> 00:00:19,653
I should stop talking, but I can't.

8
00:00:20,988 --> 00:00:22,789
I mean exactly what I said.

9
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:27,961
Lately, I keep…

10
00:00:39,273 --> 00:00:43,177
Lately, I keep dealing with situations
where I need someone to help me.

11
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:47,288
Why don't you work with me?

12
00:00:47,312 --> 00:00:48,919
Right by my side.

13
00:00:58,125 --> 00:01:00,260
Yeong Su! This is unbelievable!

14
00:01:00,761 --> 00:01:01,695
What? What is it now?

15
00:01:01,762 --> 00:01:03,931
Well, Mu I is outside right now...

16
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:05,966
Outside?

17
00:01:05,966 --> 00:01:08,302
He just offered a public job proposal!

18
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,437
What? A public proposal?

19
00:01:10,671 --> 00:01:13,407
No, idiot! A public job proposal!

20
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:16,577
"Be my staff," or something like that?

21
00:01:19,112 --> 00:01:20,147
Where is he?

22
00:01:20,981 --> 00:01:22,316
So now…

23
00:01:22,382 --> 00:01:24,918
people are asking me
if I'm about to be unemployed.

24
00:01:25,619 --> 00:01:26,620
Tell me.

25
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:28,589
Am I about to get fired?

26
00:01:31,325 --> 00:01:32,392
Well…

27
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,194
The thing is,

28
00:01:35,829 --> 00:01:38,966
you've gone so long without
a road manager,

29
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,035
so I thought it might be helpful…

30
00:01:43,036 --> 00:01:44,004
Someone to assist me?

31
00:01:44,605 --> 00:01:45,906
So it was purely for my sake,

32
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,908
just a genuine job offer?

33
00:01:48,475 --> 00:01:50,077
Yeah, exactly.

34
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:54,081
Do I look like an idiot?

35
00:01:54,348 --> 00:01:56,683
You pulled a stunt like that
without even talking to me?

36
00:01:58,886 --> 00:02:01,522
Fine! I just needed a quick way out.
So what?

37
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:04,224
Did you actually confess your feelings
or something?

38
00:02:05,559 --> 00:02:06,894
Well, not quite a confession.

39
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:09,930
I said it bothered me that she came
with Chef Kang,

40
00:02:11,031 --> 00:02:12,733
and asked if she'd stay by my side.

41
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:17,971
Mu I… Tak Mu I!

42
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:19,806
You confessed your feelings, you idiot!

43
00:02:25,245 --> 00:02:26,547
Hey, do you think she knows?

44
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:29,449
Relax. If a smart girl
like Da Hong fell for it,

45
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,151
Yu Il probably…

46
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,454
took it as a job offer as well.

47
00:02:36,123 --> 00:02:37,124
You think so?

48
00:02:38,392 --> 00:02:39,927
Yeah, I'm sure she did.

49
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:43,664
Anyway, first things first,
you need to see this.

50
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:45,432
Not sure if we can call this a scandal.

51
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:47,768
Who? Me?

52
00:02:47,968 --> 00:02:49,203
Well, who else? Me?

53
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:52,339
What? Was I photographed with Kkong?

54
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:56,643
Nothing's even happened between us yet!

55
00:02:56,643 --> 00:02:59,213
Just look at it, idiot.
Look at this, then talk.

56
00:02:59,213 --> 00:03:00,647
Stop crying already! Stop it!

57
00:03:00,714 --> 00:03:01,648
Here, look.

58
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,785
(Actor Tak Mu I, Rumored to Be Dating
a Man This Time?)

59
00:03:07,421 --> 00:03:08,422
What is this?

60
00:03:13,594 --> 00:03:14,561
(You have a message.)

61
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:15,529
(Chef, it's Producer Shin Yeong Il of ABS.
I'm writing about a program proposal…)

62
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:16,597
("Is Your Fridge Doing Well?"
Screenwriter Kang Bo Ra here.)

63
00:03:16,597 --> 00:03:17,564
(Please pick up the phone.)

64
00:03:17,564 --> 00:03:20,033
(Looks like you have a lot of time
on your hands.)

65
00:03:21,735 --> 00:03:23,770
(Actor Tak Mu I, Rumored to Be Dating
a Man This Time?)

66
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:25,873
(Seen in a sweet exchange with a man
at a premiere)

67
00:03:28,542 --> 00:03:29,710
What'd you say on stage?

68
00:03:38,085 --> 00:03:39,620
What on earth is this?

69
00:03:41,488 --> 00:03:43,624
It's not from me,
though I bet you hoped it was.

70
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,026
Yu Il felt too shy to give it
to you herself.

71
00:03:56,837 --> 00:03:58,939
So it wasn't that big a deal?

72
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,841
I thought maybe you said,

73
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:03,744
"I love you. You are so darn cool."

74
00:04:04,311 --> 00:04:05,512
Something like that?

75
00:04:16,857 --> 00:04:17,891
Can't you just…

76
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:25,098
stay by my side?

77
00:04:34,341 --> 00:04:36,844
He probably just said that
because he was drunk.

78
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:46,954
Was he confessing how he felt about me?

79
00:04:52,226 --> 00:04:53,527
Yeah, I'm losing it.

80
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:57,264
A confession? May as well write a script.

81
00:04:57,998 --> 00:04:59,967
So the genre is horror?

82
00:05:00,834 --> 00:05:01,802
What?

83
00:05:09,743 --> 00:05:10,878
I'm sorry.

84
00:05:15,115 --> 00:05:16,083
Yu Il.

85
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:17,518
What are you doing tomorrow afternoon?

86
00:05:17,851 --> 00:05:18,819
Do you have another part-time job?

87
00:05:19,553 --> 00:05:21,054
No, I don't.

88
00:05:22,122 --> 00:05:26,460
Then do you want another gig
before you start your shift?

89
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:31,832
(We support the cast and crew
of "Rooftop Romance")

90
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:38,138
(From Ryu Min the singer
to Ryu Min the actor!)

91
00:05:50,584 --> 00:05:51,552
Chef.

92
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:55,522
It doesn't look like Ryu Min will be
on set today, though.

93
00:05:58,825 --> 00:05:59,826
I know, right?

94
00:06:04,498 --> 00:06:07,701
What do you, what do you
What do you mean? Energy

95
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:09,937
Hey. Here, drink this.

96
00:06:10,504 --> 00:06:11,972
Hurry, drink up. Quick.

97
00:06:15,776 --> 00:06:16,677
Absolute nuisance.

98
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:19,012
Are you okay?

99
00:06:19,146 --> 00:06:21,682
How can he be?
A lightweight drank like a heavyweight.

100
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:24,318
Where on earth did his manager go?

101
00:06:25,052 --> 00:06:27,221
If you're a lightweight,
you should've held back.

102
00:06:29,523 --> 00:06:31,625
Chef, you're close with Min, right?

103
00:06:32,593 --> 00:06:33,660
Yes, we're close.

104
00:06:34,094 --> 00:06:36,830
You know you could send a coffee truck
to the set at some point.

105
00:06:36,864 --> 00:06:39,333
You haven't yet,
but the shoot is almost over.

106
00:06:41,835 --> 00:06:44,571
- Want me to?
- Why even ask? Of course he'd love it.

107
00:06:45,038 --> 00:06:47,641
How about in two days?
We're shooting a major scene.

108
00:06:47,975 --> 00:06:50,110
Min would love it if you came yourself.

109
00:06:51,778 --> 00:06:52,980
I see.

110
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:55,148
Looks like Da Hong was mistaken.

111
00:06:55,816 --> 00:06:57,718
She wasn't. She used us.

112
00:06:58,719 --> 00:07:01,021
What do you mean, "She used us?"

113
00:07:02,556 --> 00:07:03,590
It's a long story.

114
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:05,425
And one more thing.

115
00:07:06,093 --> 00:07:09,563
Yu Il has to be there too. She has to.

116
00:07:17,204 --> 00:07:18,805
Aren't you getting anything?
The coffee truck is here.

117
00:07:19,573 --> 00:07:21,875
I'm not going. I mean, I can't.

118
00:07:22,476 --> 00:07:24,178
You said Kkong is here too.

119
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,146
I'm too embarrassed to face her.

120
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,447
Right, of course.

121
00:07:27,681 --> 00:07:30,584
If she asked, "When should I get started,"

122
00:07:30,584 --> 00:07:31,518
that would be awkward.

123
00:07:31,852 --> 00:07:33,387
Why did it have to be today?

124
00:07:34,154 --> 00:07:36,390
Why did it have to be today of all days?

125
00:07:37,658 --> 00:07:40,360
That chef really rubs me the wrong way.

126
00:07:43,363 --> 00:07:45,098
- Take good care of Min.
- Thank you.

127
00:07:45,098 --> 00:07:46,266
Sure, enjoy.

128
00:07:46,266 --> 00:07:47,434
Take good care of Min.

129
00:07:47,768 --> 00:07:49,736
You're so quick.

130
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:53,273
Starbucks, Coffee Bean, Mega Coffee,
and Mammoth Coffee.

131
00:07:53,307 --> 00:07:55,642
I've worked in coffee shops for years.

132
00:07:58,412 --> 00:07:59,446
Here's your coffee.

133
00:07:59,446 --> 00:08:00,480
Thank you.

134
00:08:01,782 --> 00:08:03,450
He doesn't eat whipped cream…

135
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:04,451
What do I do?

136
00:08:05,352 --> 00:08:07,354
- Hey, there you are.
- Hey, bro.

137
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:11,592
Thanks, Hee Su. Really.

138
00:08:11,892 --> 00:08:14,061
But they said you weren't
on the schedule today.

139
00:08:14,194 --> 00:08:15,395
Yeah, exactly.

140
00:08:15,395 --> 00:08:17,130
I ran over to find out what's going on.

141
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:19,333
You really didn't have to come over.

142
00:08:19,366 --> 00:08:22,236
With all the calls and texts,
I figured I'd better show up.

143
00:08:23,537 --> 00:08:26,573
Still, it's nice to see the face
of the person the coffee truck is for.

144
00:08:26,607 --> 00:08:29,109
Then could you make me a hot latte?

145
00:08:29,176 --> 00:08:31,111
Of course, one latte coming up.

146
00:08:35,449 --> 00:08:37,684
So I heard you're not
actually a fan of mine.

147
00:08:41,722 --> 00:08:43,690
I'm sorry. It was actually my friend…

148
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,527
Let's have tea with your friend sometime.

149
00:08:47,327 --> 00:08:48,328
Really?

150
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:50,464
She'll be so happy.

151
00:08:50,731 --> 00:08:52,833
- Thank you.
- It's nothing…

152
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,501
Hello, Chef!

153
00:08:54,525 --> 00:08:55,617
Hi, Yu Il!

154
00:08:55,642 --> 00:08:56,743
Hi.

155
00:08:56,803 --> 00:09:00,841
- You did this for a reason, didn't you?
- No, I just got the dates wrong.

156
00:09:01,241 --> 00:09:02,976
Da Hong, do you want anything?

157
00:09:03,911 --> 00:09:06,013
I haven't had anything, so I am hungry.

158
00:09:06,847 --> 00:09:09,316
Then shall I make you a latte?

159
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,554
It's okay. I don't want coffee breath.

160
00:09:14,221 --> 00:09:16,557
I'm shooting a kissing scene today.

161
00:09:18,325 --> 00:09:20,194
Really? With whom?

162
00:09:20,627 --> 00:09:22,796
Who else? Mu I.

163
00:09:23,764 --> 00:09:25,933
Bye, Yu Il. Have fun, everyone!

164
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:27,208
Good luck.

165
00:09:45,185 --> 00:09:46,753
(Rooting for you!)

166
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:47,855
So sweet of her.

167
00:09:51,491 --> 00:09:54,695
Wait, she's rooting for the kissing scene?

168
00:10:16,817 --> 00:10:19,686
You're staring at my employee
for a little too long.

169
00:10:20,787 --> 00:10:23,924
You're being a little overprotective,
don't you think?

170
00:10:23,991 --> 00:10:25,158
Well, who knows?

171
00:10:25,592 --> 00:10:28,262
She's so efficient at her job.
We might have her stay on…

172
00:10:28,929 --> 00:10:29,897
by my side.

173
00:10:33,834 --> 00:10:35,769
So you're shooting
a major scene today, yes?

174
00:10:36,336 --> 00:10:37,571
Yeah, you're right.

175
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:40,474
It's such an important scene,
and I need to focus.

176
00:10:41,341 --> 00:10:43,377
Why is the truck still here
if the job is done?

177
00:10:44,411 --> 00:10:47,381
Because it'd be a shame
to miss a good show.

178
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:53,921
I think a lot of people hope
the two of us get together.

179
00:10:54,454 --> 00:10:55,556
Come to the restaurant.

180
00:10:56,023 --> 00:10:58,559
I'll prepare a delicious meal for you,
made with care.

181
00:10:59,526 --> 00:11:00,827
I'm sorry,

182
00:11:00,961 --> 00:11:03,997
but 365 days a year, I watch my diet…

183
00:11:04,431 --> 00:11:05,432
with care.

184
00:11:05,432 --> 00:11:08,669
Then I'll put together
a special diet menu.

185
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:10,304
If that's what you want, babe.

186
00:11:10,938 --> 00:11:12,239
"Babe," my foot.

187
00:11:12,973 --> 00:11:14,474
We're about to shoot!

188
00:11:16,743 --> 00:11:17,711
Good luck, babe.

189
00:11:20,948 --> 00:11:22,549
He makes my skin crawl.

190
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:26,920
Okay, get ready!

191
00:11:27,454 --> 00:11:29,523
And action!

192
00:11:31,091 --> 00:11:33,360
Did you mean what you said on the phone?

193
00:11:35,395 --> 00:11:37,965
If you still feel the same about me.

194
00:11:39,766 --> 00:11:42,669
Then I'm doing things
my way from now on, okay?

195
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:05,926
Cut!

196
00:12:17,838 --> 00:12:21,108
Director, Mu I's eyelashes
are trembling a lot.

197
00:12:21,108 --> 00:12:23,677
Right? Let's go again.

198
00:12:24,144 --> 00:12:25,245
What's this?

199
00:12:25,245 --> 00:12:27,814
This is making you nervous too,
right, Mu I?

200
00:12:28,215 --> 00:12:29,850
I know you can do well.

201
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:32,719
- Want to take a break if you're nervous?
- No!

202
00:12:33,287 --> 00:12:36,590
The sunlight is just too strong.
Let's just do another take now.

203
00:12:37,691 --> 00:12:39,359
Okay, let's go again!

204
00:12:39,693 --> 00:12:42,229
Okay, the lines were good.
Let's just do the kissing scene.

205
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:45,265
Okay, and…

206
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,467
action!

207
00:13:15,729 --> 00:13:16,697
Cut!

208
00:13:18,699 --> 00:13:19,666
That was good.

209
00:13:29,076 --> 00:13:30,143
It's over.

210
00:13:30,944 --> 00:13:32,946
It's not like we're watching
a horror movie.

211
00:13:34,014 --> 00:13:35,782
No, it's just…

212
00:13:35,782 --> 00:13:38,619
it's embarrassing to see it for real.

213
00:13:39,353 --> 00:13:41,088
Sure, we've all felt envious before.

214
00:13:42,022 --> 00:13:44,391
No, I said "embarrassed."

215
00:13:44,858 --> 00:13:47,895
Yeah, I'm envious too. Now I really want
to be in a relationship.

216
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:54,902
- Are you feeling envious?
- No, I'm really not.

217
00:13:58,572 --> 00:14:01,108
This time, let's go tight
on the lips one more time.

218
00:14:01,241 --> 00:14:02,209
Okay.

219
00:14:04,144 --> 00:14:06,280
- Drive safely.
- Bye-bye.

220
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:24,998
Yu Il, one second.

221
00:14:31,572 --> 00:14:32,539
Get in.

222
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,726
- Thank you.
- I'm closing the door.

223
00:14:34,751 --> 00:14:35,620
Okay.

224
00:14:44,418 --> 00:14:45,705
Have a good day, babe.

225
00:14:53,227 --> 00:14:54,528
That jerk, seriously…

226
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,432
- Hang in there, babe.
- "Babe," my foot.

227
00:15:04,338 --> 00:15:06,039
Still thinking about that horror movie?

228
00:15:07,241 --> 00:15:08,709
No, I'm not.

229
00:15:10,844 --> 00:15:13,680
Do you want to go see
a really scary movie together?

230
00:15:14,515 --> 00:15:15,482
What?

231
00:15:15,482 --> 00:15:19,353
I'm good at eating,
drinking, and sleeping alone.

232
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,488
I'm good at doing everything solo,

233
00:15:21,688 --> 00:15:24,858
but I can't watch movies alone,
especially scary ones.

234
00:15:27,327 --> 00:15:29,663
You don't seem like the type
who can't watch horror films.

235
00:15:30,631 --> 00:15:32,432
Well, that's true…

236
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:34,034
So let's go together.

237
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:39,606
It may be hard to find
the time to do that…

238
00:15:40,507 --> 00:15:43,744
Is it hard to find the time, or is it hard
to have the heart to want it?

239
00:15:50,584 --> 00:15:51,618
Here you are.

240
00:15:54,755 --> 00:15:56,123
Thank you for the meal, Auntie.

241
00:15:56,356 --> 00:15:58,091
- Eat plenty.
- Yes, ma'am.

242
00:15:58,859 --> 00:16:00,294
Why are there flowers, anyway?

243
00:16:00,294 --> 00:16:02,429
You never bring fans' gifts home.

244
00:16:02,996 --> 00:16:05,599
Someone special gave me these.
Pretty, right?

245
00:16:05,599 --> 00:16:07,201
Yes, they're pretty.

246
00:16:07,201 --> 00:16:08,969
They really brighten up the house.

247
00:16:10,437 --> 00:16:11,805
Then I'll head out now, okay?

248
00:16:12,139 --> 00:16:14,408
Yes, sorry for the late hour.

249
00:16:14,441 --> 00:16:17,878
I really wanted Auntie's cooking today
because I haven't had it in a while.

250
00:16:18,412 --> 00:16:19,947
It's fine. I'm glad you called.

251
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,583
Don't do the dishes.
Just leave them to soak.

252
00:16:22,649 --> 00:16:24,785
- I'll come tomorrow and do it.
- Okay.

253
00:16:25,118 --> 00:16:27,221
- Have a good time.
- I will. Thank you.

254
00:16:27,221 --> 00:16:28,188
I'll see you.

255
00:16:28,188 --> 00:16:29,256
- Take care.
- Okay.

256
00:16:31,425 --> 00:16:34,628
Wait, all this time, you eat meals
like this and don't gain weight?

257
00:16:35,696 --> 00:16:36,697
Why did you come?

258
00:16:36,897 --> 00:16:38,966
I heard your housekeeper's cooking
is great,

259
00:16:39,466 --> 00:16:40,467
so I came to try it.

260
00:16:42,769 --> 00:16:46,473
Someone stricter than me about weight
gain comes to eat with me at this hour.

261
00:16:46,473 --> 00:16:47,841
You expect me to believe that?

262
00:16:51,812 --> 00:16:52,846
Let's talk first.

263
00:16:55,949 --> 00:16:56,950
It's nothing, really…

264
00:16:57,818 --> 00:17:01,121
When I was watching the kissing scene
earlier, I got curious.

265
00:17:01,688 --> 00:17:02,656
About what?

266
00:17:03,190 --> 00:17:07,060
Whether a scene that’s all acting
is really just acting…

267
00:17:07,895 --> 00:17:11,398
or the acting can turn into real feelings
as time passes.

268
00:17:14,301 --> 00:17:16,436
- It's not like that.
- What?

269
00:17:16,503 --> 00:17:19,039
It's really not like that
between Da Hong and me.

270
00:17:19,673 --> 00:17:21,108
But Da Hong likes you…

271
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:26,480
To Da Hong, I'm her emotional sustenance.

272
00:17:29,183 --> 00:17:31,185
Da Hong has been lonely
since she was little.

273
00:17:32,052 --> 00:17:33,120
So was I.

274
00:17:34,221 --> 00:17:37,024
Even as a kid, she was smart enough
to find a kindred spirit.

275
00:17:38,025 --> 00:17:38,992
Her own camouflage.

276
00:17:40,227 --> 00:17:42,496
She hid behind me, so no one would
see the real her.

277
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:46,066
Ever since then,
she's shown me total devotion,

278
00:17:47,568 --> 00:17:50,070
but it was all to protect her own heart.

279
00:17:53,674 --> 00:17:55,676
Are you sure about that?

280
00:17:58,645 --> 00:17:59,680
Tell her how you feel.

281
00:18:00,981 --> 00:18:02,649
So our "hungry" friend can also see…

282
00:18:03,083 --> 00:18:04,834
that besides her current sustenance,

283
00:18:04,901 --> 00:18:06,653
something else can fill her heart.

284
00:18:08,589 --> 00:18:10,257
Well, what if we can't even be friends?

285
00:18:11,959 --> 00:18:13,527
That's her choice. What about you?

286
00:18:14,161 --> 00:18:15,204
Are you fine with it?

287
00:18:15,229 --> 00:18:18,532
Watching Da Hong's kissing scene
earlier, my insides just…

288
00:18:18,799 --> 00:18:20,267
But I want to see her so badly…

289
00:18:22,669 --> 00:18:23,637
right now…

290
00:18:25,172 --> 00:18:27,908
Look, there's still quite a lot
left to shoot,

291
00:18:28,575 --> 00:18:29,643
and most importantly,

292
00:18:30,711 --> 00:18:32,145
Da Hong's heart is with you.

293
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:39,586
Then put the confession on hold
and take it one step at a time.

294
00:18:40,287 --> 00:18:43,156
If you want to see her, do so.
If you want to eat with her, say so.

295
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:49,596
Yeah, that's all it takes.

296
00:18:50,931 --> 00:18:51,899
What?

297
00:18:53,267 --> 00:18:54,242
No, never mind.

298
00:18:54,267 --> 00:18:55,782
Min, eat quickly before it gets cold.

299
00:19:16,924 --> 00:19:18,559
Why did my heart race like that?

300
00:19:19,059 --> 00:19:21,028
It's not my first time
watching a kissing scene.

301
00:20:01,301 --> 00:20:03,770
What on earth? I'm losing it!

302
00:20:05,239 --> 00:20:06,773
Why did I close my eyes?

303
00:20:07,541 --> 00:20:09,042
Why was I on my tiptoes?

304
00:20:11,979 --> 00:20:13,780
This is why I shouldn't watch dramas.

305
00:20:23,357 --> 00:20:26,460
If it's not too late,
can we meet for a bit right now?

306
00:20:27,294 --> 00:20:28,829
I'd like to go somewhere with you.

307
00:20:28,862 --> 00:20:33,107
(Tak Mu I)

308
00:20:37,037 --> 00:20:40,007
Excuse me… Do you have time?

309
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:41,875
You scared me!

310
00:20:43,177 --> 00:20:45,712
What happened?
I thought you'd come by car.

311
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:48,982
I ate late, so I wanted to walk.

312
00:20:49,950 --> 00:20:52,586
I assume this isn't the place
you wanted to go.

313
00:20:53,754 --> 00:20:54,755
Not here.

314
00:20:55,322 --> 00:20:57,157
There's a place we have to go.

315
00:20:57,991 --> 00:21:01,862
Is that so? Then lead the way.

316
00:21:04,598 --> 00:21:06,033
Look ahead!

317
00:21:10,604 --> 00:21:14,074
- Why do you keep turning around?
- To see if you're keeping up.

318
00:21:16,276 --> 00:21:17,311
Excuse me!

319
00:21:20,147 --> 00:21:21,849
Can we talk for a moment?

320
00:21:23,417 --> 00:21:24,785
What about?

321
00:21:25,752 --> 00:21:27,254
Have you ever thought about modeling?

322
00:21:32,025 --> 00:21:35,929
What do you do?
You have amazing proportions.

323
00:21:37,464 --> 00:21:38,465
Ma'am, it's…

324
00:21:38,765 --> 00:21:41,301
Could you show me your face?

325
00:21:41,401 --> 00:21:43,971
I can tell your face
is totally model material too.

326
00:21:43,971 --> 00:21:45,806
Should I do something?

327
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:50,010
- Would you consider auditioning?
- No, thank you.

328
00:21:50,244 --> 00:21:53,280
- Come on, let me see your face…
- Excuse me…

329
00:21:54,081 --> 00:21:57,150
I'm sorry,
but you really shouldn't be doing this.

330
00:21:57,184 --> 00:21:58,151
What?

331
00:21:58,485 --> 00:22:00,554
He already belongs to an agency.

332
00:22:00,954 --> 00:22:03,423
He's a rookie we've put a lot of effort
into preparing.

333
00:22:05,859 --> 00:22:08,161
Then you should've said so from the start.

334
00:22:09,396 --> 00:22:10,464
Which agency is it?

335
00:22:10,664 --> 00:22:12,733
You wouldn't know it. It's new.

336
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:14,301
Right.

337
00:22:14,501 --> 00:22:16,837
No way someone like him
would've gone unnoticed.

338
00:22:18,172 --> 00:22:19,139
It's too bad.

339
00:22:19,773 --> 00:22:21,141
It's such a shame!

340
00:22:25,712 --> 00:22:27,848
Would you say that she has an eye…

341
00:22:27,848 --> 00:22:30,284
for picking someone
out of the crowd or not?

342
00:22:30,717 --> 00:22:31,685
Good point.

343
00:22:32,152 --> 00:22:34,388
(Only one person per batting cage)

344
00:22:34,388 --> 00:22:36,390
(Cards accepted inside the batting cage)

345
00:22:37,224 --> 00:22:39,259
Baseball now? At this hour?

346
00:22:39,284 --> 00:22:40,803
It's only empty if we come at this hour.

347
00:22:41,562 --> 00:22:45,132
- Well, it does sound fun.
- I'll teach you…

348
00:22:46,867 --> 00:22:50,003
Want to make a bet?
How about the loser buys drinks?

349
00:22:51,371 --> 00:22:52,873
Let's say the winner buys.

350
00:22:53,841 --> 00:22:55,742
Well, that works too.

351
00:22:58,078 --> 00:23:00,280
But I don't have any coins.

352
00:23:06,687 --> 00:23:07,654
Here!

353
00:23:29,476 --> 00:23:30,878
Yu Il, stand here.

354
00:23:31,044 --> 00:23:32,880
Spread your feet a bit, and hold the bat.

355
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:36,450
Left hand on the bottom,
right hand on top.

356
00:23:37,017 --> 00:23:38,952
Grip it. Are you holding it tightly?

357
00:23:39,987 --> 00:23:41,755
Then, you go like this.

358
00:23:42,089 --> 00:23:44,157
When the ball comes, one, two.

359
00:23:47,528 --> 00:23:49,296
Again, lift it up.

360
00:24:05,279 --> 00:24:07,948
- Did you see that?
- Have you done this before?

361
00:24:08,348 --> 00:24:09,783
I was terrible at first,

362
00:24:09,783 --> 00:24:12,686
but whenever I was stressed,
I came here, tried it, and got better.

363
00:24:12,953 --> 00:24:14,388
Okay, now it's Mr. Tak's turn.

364
00:24:27,601 --> 00:24:28,869
What's this?

365
00:24:35,976 --> 00:24:37,010
What was that?

366
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:41,148
Here.

367
00:24:44,051 --> 00:24:46,420
- We have to do this another time.
- I said okay.

368
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:48,121
That's the fifth time you've said that.

369
00:24:48,655 --> 00:24:51,925
- Promise me, okay? Promise!
- Yes, sir. Will do.

370
00:24:53,427 --> 00:24:54,461
Thanks for the drink.

371
00:25:05,806 --> 00:25:08,141
There are still times
I can't get used to this.

372
00:25:08,709 --> 00:25:10,777
Drinking coffee
with the coffee brand model.

373
00:25:11,778 --> 00:25:14,515
What does it feel like to drink
something with your face on it?

374
00:25:15,549 --> 00:25:16,583
Hard to say.

375
00:25:17,217 --> 00:25:18,318
I'm just used to it.

376
00:25:19,786 --> 00:25:22,189
I don't think I'd ever get used to it.

377
00:25:22,723 --> 00:25:23,590
What?

378
00:25:24,191 --> 00:25:27,127
I'm only a job seeker, and here I am…

379
00:25:29,229 --> 00:25:31,598
Anyway, it's just unreal.

380
00:25:32,499 --> 00:25:33,800
Why is it unreal?

381
00:25:36,036 --> 00:25:39,139
We're sitting right here
side by side, aren't we?

382
00:25:43,510 --> 00:25:48,849
I can't explain it, but it just is.

383
00:25:54,955 --> 00:25:56,623
I can touch your hand like this.

384
00:26:01,128 --> 00:26:02,729
I can touch your hair like this.

385
00:26:05,499 --> 00:26:07,034
Am I still unreal to you?

386
00:26:19,913 --> 00:26:22,749
Hey, Yeong Su. What?

387
00:26:23,417 --> 00:26:25,252
(Gangseong General Hospital)

388
00:26:27,154 --> 00:26:28,188
Are you really okay?

389
00:26:29,256 --> 00:26:32,059
I said I'm fine.
Thankfully, I had my seatbelt on.

390
00:26:32,326 --> 00:26:33,427
Are you sure you're really okay?

391
00:26:33,894 --> 00:26:35,429
Other than my heart…

392
00:26:35,729 --> 00:26:37,865
pounding from the shock, I'm fine.

393
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,901
Tell me the details.

394
00:26:41,502 --> 00:26:43,504
Well, since you have
an early shoot tomorrow,

395
00:26:43,504 --> 00:26:46,607
I was going to your place to sleep over,
and on my way there…

396
00:27:02,589 --> 00:27:03,590
What on earth?

397
00:27:17,838 --> 00:27:19,740
Blood! It's blood!

398
00:27:20,874 --> 00:27:22,776
You must've been so shocked.

399
00:27:22,976 --> 00:27:24,511
Thank goodness it wasn't worse.

400
00:27:24,511 --> 00:27:27,881
But this doesn't seem like a coincidence.

401
00:27:27,881 --> 00:27:29,983
And there was that incident
with Yu Il before.

402
00:27:31,118 --> 00:27:32,152
What about the dashcam?

403
00:27:32,152 --> 00:27:33,854
The police took it at the scene.

404
00:27:34,021 --> 00:27:35,923
Something should turn up by tomorrow.

405
00:27:36,290 --> 00:27:39,493
It couldn't be that woman
from before, could it?

406
00:27:41,261 --> 00:27:44,731
But on the dashcam, I caught a glimpse…

407
00:27:45,933 --> 00:27:48,669
of a woman with long hair on the overpass.

408
00:27:52,639 --> 00:27:54,975
I have something to tell you.

409
00:27:57,377 --> 00:27:59,947
The day we drank beer by the Han River,

410
00:28:00,414 --> 00:28:02,616
I went down to return your card wallet,

411
00:28:02,983 --> 00:28:05,652
and I bumped into a woman
in front of my building,

412
00:28:05,819 --> 00:28:08,322
like she came over
to bump into me on purpose.

413
00:28:10,544 --> 00:28:12,593
So that's why you wanted
to come here with me.

414
00:28:13,527 --> 00:28:15,462
Were you hurt at the time?

415
00:28:16,797 --> 00:28:18,832
Thankfully, no.

416
00:28:19,533 --> 00:28:21,235
But out of nowhere,

417
00:28:21,235 --> 00:28:24,137
she asked me if I had a boyfriend.

418
00:28:24,872 --> 00:28:26,707
Did you see her face?

419
00:28:27,641 --> 00:28:29,510
I didn't…

420
00:28:31,211 --> 00:28:33,046
But one thing's for sure,

421
00:28:33,380 --> 00:28:35,115
she had long hair.

422
00:28:35,382 --> 00:28:36,550
Like Song Yun O?

423
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:42,356
By any chance, were you two…

424
00:28:42,356 --> 00:28:43,924
talking about something?

425
00:28:44,525 --> 00:28:45,592
Why?

426
00:28:45,592 --> 00:28:48,362
Because it looked like someone
was listening in outside the door.

427
00:29:03,277 --> 00:29:05,445
Was it something people
shouldn't have heard?

428
00:29:05,779 --> 00:29:08,682
- Did she have long hair?
- No, it was a man.

429
00:29:08,882 --> 00:29:09,850
A man?

430
00:29:09,850 --> 00:29:12,786
You idiot, in a hospital,
the emergency exit is a loudspeaker.

431
00:29:12,786 --> 00:29:15,522
Secret dates or consultations,
everything turns into rumors.

432
00:29:16,490 --> 00:29:19,159
We're not in a relationship or anything.

433
00:29:19,193 --> 00:29:22,496
Other than that night,
we didn't really talk about anything.

434
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:24,998
"That night?"

435
00:29:25,165 --> 00:29:26,567
No, it's not like that.

436
00:29:27,768 --> 00:29:29,837
Even if it's not, you should introduce us.

437
00:29:30,237 --> 00:29:32,206
Hello, I'm Yoon Jae Gyu.

438
00:29:32,206 --> 00:29:34,608
I was once a child actor, now a doctor.

439
00:29:34,808 --> 00:29:36,176
We've met before, right?

440
00:29:38,412 --> 00:29:41,048
At that coffee incident. I was there, too.

441
00:29:41,148 --> 00:29:42,883
I'm sorry,

442
00:29:42,883 --> 00:29:45,519
I was too flustered to recognize you then.

443
00:29:46,119 --> 00:29:48,555
Did it leave a scar?

444
00:29:49,356 --> 00:29:52,259
No, I put on ointment as instructed.

445
00:29:52,893 --> 00:29:55,863
Did you enjoy your meal
at the fine dining restaurant?

446
00:29:56,630 --> 00:29:57,831
Sorry?

447
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:01,101
Yes.

448
00:30:03,103 --> 00:30:06,106
- Looks like I've found her.
- Aren't you busy?

449
00:30:10,210 --> 00:30:11,945
(Gangjung Police Station)

450
00:30:12,045 --> 00:30:13,981
Hey, that's all there is.

451
00:30:14,114 --> 00:30:16,016
That Song Yun O woman,

452
00:30:16,250 --> 00:30:18,151
she got off with a summary fine,

453
00:30:18,151 --> 00:30:19,586
and that was the end of it.

454
00:30:20,087 --> 00:30:22,990
So the woman who got attacked at the time
wasn't Tak Mu I's girl?

455
00:30:22,990 --> 00:30:24,157
Nope.

456
00:30:24,791 --> 00:30:28,328
She went to the set with her friend
and got caught up in that mess.

457
00:30:29,663 --> 00:30:32,866
They say her friend is
a producer for Tak Mu I's show.

458
00:30:32,866 --> 00:30:35,235
So that's how they met?

459
00:30:35,602 --> 00:30:36,737
Sir,

460
00:30:37,437 --> 00:30:38,972
they say it's nothing much.

461
00:30:38,972 --> 00:30:41,074
- It's not that stalker from before.
- Is that so?

462
00:30:41,074 --> 00:30:44,077
They're analyzing nearby
security footage, so they said to wait.

463
00:30:44,144 --> 00:30:45,479
Okay, thank you.

464
00:30:46,713 --> 00:30:47,814
So that's it.

465
00:30:47,814 --> 00:30:49,082
Tak Mu I's manager's accident.

466
00:30:49,950 --> 00:30:52,352
Hey, how much do you already know?

467
00:30:52,386 --> 00:30:54,555
I told you. I know everything.

468
00:30:54,655 --> 00:30:55,923
Just give me something.

469
00:30:55,923 --> 00:30:58,025
Your hometown buddy
is trying to make a living.

470
00:30:58,025 --> 00:30:59,960
Forget it, it's confidential.

471
00:31:00,460 --> 00:31:03,230
Even though the case is small,

472
00:31:03,230 --> 00:31:04,932
there's a big law firm involved,

473
00:31:04,932 --> 00:31:07,034
which means it could get messy
if we're careless.

474
00:31:07,034 --> 00:31:08,869
I said I'll protect my source.

475
00:31:08,869 --> 00:31:10,003
Come on, man.

476
00:31:10,003 --> 00:31:11,083
Come on, bro!

477
00:31:11,107 --> 00:31:12,621
Are you really
going to be like this?

478
00:31:13,073 --> 00:31:15,209
Hey, you start speaking
in our regional dialect…

479
00:31:15,209 --> 00:31:17,411
and get clingy
only when you need something.

480
00:31:17,444 --> 00:31:21,615
Last time, you caught that musician
who was using propofol, thanks to me.

481
00:31:23,250 --> 00:31:24,718
Fine, okay.

482
00:31:25,285 --> 00:31:27,721
What? What do you want to know?

483
00:31:44,838 --> 00:31:46,573
I hope he got home okay yesterday.

484
00:31:47,407 --> 00:31:50,844
He's as tall as a door.
He must stand out to people.

485
00:31:55,048 --> 00:31:56,350
Come on, Gong Yu Il.

486
00:31:57,951 --> 00:32:00,053
Who is worrying about whom?

487
00:32:00,988 --> 00:32:04,224
I can't believe I'm worried
about a celebrity. This is ridiculous.

488
00:32:07,294 --> 00:32:09,463
Did I just become a Tak Mu I fan?

489
00:32:10,757 --> 00:32:12,399
Am I falling for Tak Mu I now?

490
00:32:19,439 --> 00:32:21,975
Thanks for the meal today.
I'll treat you tomorrow.

491
00:32:21,975 --> 00:32:22,943
(Yo Daily News)

492
00:32:22,943 --> 00:32:24,578
What are you doing? What's that?

493
00:32:25,679 --> 00:32:28,515
What's with the scrambling?
What was that about?

494
00:32:28,749 --> 00:32:30,617
Were you watching something naughty?

495
00:32:31,652 --> 00:32:32,753
It's not like that.

496
00:32:32,819 --> 00:32:33,948
Hey, if you've got something good,

497
00:32:33,973 --> 00:32:35,913
share it with me, as a colleague.

498
00:32:36,490 --> 00:32:39,793
Mr. Park, I think I have to go
out of town for a story.

499
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,328
Out of town? Why?

500
00:32:41,662 --> 00:32:44,565
Hey, you'll come up empty anyway.
Why bother going out of town?

501
00:32:44,831 --> 00:32:46,033
I'll be back.

502
00:32:47,367 --> 00:32:48,402
Fine.

503
00:33:07,754 --> 00:33:09,156
Look at this guy.

504
00:33:17,598 --> 00:33:19,266
Welcome in.

505
00:33:19,266 --> 00:33:20,834
Excuse me, Miss Song Yun O?

506
00:33:28,442 --> 00:33:30,143
Miss Song, just a minute.

507
00:33:30,143 --> 00:33:31,278
Excuse me, Miss Song.

508
00:33:31,478 --> 00:33:32,813
I told you to get lost.

509
00:33:32,980 --> 00:33:36,483
You've been misunderstood and wronged.
I won't take up much of your time.

510
00:33:37,551 --> 00:33:39,653
If you talk to me now,
once you return as an actor,

511
00:33:39,653 --> 00:33:41,755
I'll write a nice article for you,
I promise.

512
00:33:53,033 --> 00:33:54,601
Let go!

513
00:33:55,903 --> 00:33:58,138
Let go of me. Please!

514
00:33:59,173 --> 00:34:00,240
Let go!

515
00:34:04,411 --> 00:34:07,648
Help me! Please, help!

516
00:34:07,948 --> 00:34:11,585
Help me! Please, somebody, help me!

517
00:34:11,785 --> 00:34:14,288
Please, I'm begging you, help me!

518
00:34:14,354 --> 00:34:16,089
Help me!

519
00:34:26,233 --> 00:34:29,870
(Yo Daily News)

520
00:34:43,083 --> 00:34:46,153
I'm not the only one.
There are plenty besides me.

521
00:34:46,887 --> 00:34:49,756
And the ones who really
deserve punishment…

522
00:34:49,756 --> 00:34:52,359
aren't the people who follow Tak Mu I
because they love him.

523
00:34:52,359 --> 00:34:55,262
It's the wenches who use
those innocent people.

524
00:34:55,596 --> 00:34:56,864
What do you mean?

525
00:35:08,242 --> 00:35:09,376
You're early.

526
00:35:09,643 --> 00:35:11,612
I was told there would be two.
Is it just you?

527
00:35:12,145 --> 00:35:13,247
What?

528
00:35:13,881 --> 00:35:14,948
Who are you?

529
00:35:15,449 --> 00:35:18,085
Who am I? I work here.

530
00:35:19,286 --> 00:35:21,922
Anyway, what's the point of seeing
where Tak Mu I lives?

531
00:35:21,922 --> 00:35:23,257
There's nothing much.

532
00:35:24,024 --> 00:35:26,627
Anyway, I got the money.

533
00:35:28,295 --> 00:35:31,832
- You do this kind of thing for money?
- What?

534
00:35:32,099 --> 00:35:33,734
Then should I do it for free?

535
00:35:34,835 --> 00:35:36,603
I'm supposed to be on vacation,

536
00:35:36,603 --> 00:35:39,206
but I came to open the door
especially for you, miss.

537
00:35:39,206 --> 00:35:41,675
There's a lot that goes
into this arrangement.

538
00:35:42,709 --> 00:35:44,278
Anyway, go on in.

539
00:35:44,278 --> 00:35:45,879
I'll buy cigarettes and come in.

540
00:35:45,879 --> 00:35:47,881
Right, give me your phone.

541
00:35:51,585 --> 00:35:53,253
I'll give it back when you leave.

542
00:35:54,021 --> 00:35:56,523
Sure, you can look around everywhere.

543
00:35:56,523 --> 00:35:58,358
Lying on the bed?

544
00:35:59,092 --> 00:36:00,994
Fine, today that's okay.

545
00:36:00,994 --> 00:36:03,330
But anything in the house,

546
00:36:03,330 --> 00:36:05,065
you can't take any of it.

547
00:36:05,065 --> 00:36:07,367
If you do, it makes you a thief, got it?

548
00:36:07,367 --> 00:36:09,937
And of course you can't leave
anything behind either.

549
00:36:09,970 --> 00:36:11,505
There's a camera inside,

550
00:36:11,505 --> 00:36:13,340
so don't try anything weird.

551
00:36:14,808 --> 00:36:17,444
But if there's a camera,
how is this possible?

552
00:36:18,512 --> 00:36:20,447
I delete it. Only I watch the footage.

553
00:36:20,914 --> 00:36:21,915
Anyway,

554
00:36:21,915 --> 00:36:24,318
if we both want to stay alive,
what do we do?

555
00:36:24,818 --> 00:36:26,720
Keep your promise.

556
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:29,556
Okay, pinky promise like this. Promise.

557
00:36:29,556 --> 00:36:31,225
Great, go on in.

558
00:36:54,715 --> 00:36:56,016
It's so pretty.

559
00:37:08,228 --> 00:37:09,696
This is so nice.

560
00:37:19,306 --> 00:37:21,275
What? The door is open?

561
00:37:21,375 --> 00:37:22,442
What?

562
00:37:22,743 --> 00:37:26,680
Looks like the housekeeper figured we'd
be late, kept the door open, and left.

563
00:37:26,947 --> 00:37:28,515
That lady is asking for trouble.

564
00:37:29,950 --> 00:37:31,885
We don't have to see each other
in person, do we?

565
00:37:31,885 --> 00:37:32,953
Is that the manager?

566
00:37:33,187 --> 00:37:34,855
That looks like the bedroom.

567
00:37:37,257 --> 00:37:40,060
The room is huge too.

568
00:37:40,394 --> 00:37:41,895
Look at the bed.

569
00:37:41,895 --> 00:37:45,065
If he lives alone, why is his bed so big?

570
00:37:45,065 --> 00:37:46,867
Maybe he doesn't sleep alone.

571
00:37:49,303 --> 00:37:51,572
Hey, want to do it?

572
00:37:51,572 --> 00:37:54,541
- What are you saying?
- Why not? Come here.

573
00:37:55,008 --> 00:37:56,043
What's with you?

574
00:37:56,043 --> 00:37:58,979
Seriously! Stop!

575
00:38:00,013 --> 00:38:02,216
We do what we came to do
and leave fast, okay?

576
00:38:02,216 --> 00:38:03,250
Okay.

577
00:38:06,486 --> 00:38:07,855
I love it here.

578
00:38:09,957 --> 00:38:10,991
Hey!

579
00:38:16,763 --> 00:38:17,898
Hey.

580
00:38:18,699 --> 00:38:19,833
"What we came to do?"

581
00:38:21,201 --> 00:38:24,605
If that's true, Tak Mu I
could be in danger.

582
00:38:25,272 --> 00:38:26,974
Why didn't you tell the police then?

583
00:38:27,407 --> 00:38:29,710
They would've added
trespassing to the charges.

584
00:38:30,544 --> 00:38:32,746
Also, I don't even like him anymore.

585
00:38:32,746 --> 00:38:34,114
His safety isn't my concern.

586
00:38:36,483 --> 00:38:37,584
Keep your promise…

587
00:38:37,784 --> 00:38:40,020
about you writing an article
for me when I return.

588
00:38:49,062 --> 00:38:51,231
This story is going to be bigger
than I thought.

589
00:39:02,576 --> 00:39:03,577
Grandma!

590
00:39:03,577 --> 00:39:06,647
My goodness, sweetheart.

591
00:39:06,747 --> 00:39:07,748
What brings you here?

592
00:39:08,081 --> 00:39:10,217
I missed you so much I couldn't stand it,

593
00:39:10,217 --> 00:39:11,485
but you're so busy.

594
00:39:11,718 --> 00:39:13,453
Whoever wants it most
comes knocking, right?

595
00:39:13,487 --> 00:39:16,523
What can I do when I'm in such demand
even at my age?

596
00:39:16,924 --> 00:39:18,959
Right, you're so blessed.

597
00:39:19,526 --> 00:39:20,994
Don't you know?

598
00:39:21,895 --> 00:39:24,831
The only true blessing in my life is you.

599
00:39:26,867 --> 00:39:29,536
Okay, should your little
blessing run lines with you?

600
00:39:29,536 --> 00:39:30,537
Yes.

601
00:39:33,874 --> 00:39:35,843
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

602
00:39:37,444 --> 00:39:38,745
Is the setup done?

603
00:39:38,745 --> 00:39:39,947
Ma'am,

604
00:39:40,314 --> 00:39:43,684
I'm so, so sorry, but the schedule
just got pushed back.

605
00:39:43,684 --> 00:39:45,919
So it'd be best if you ate first
and came back…

606
00:39:45,919 --> 00:39:48,889
Really? I was hungry anyway.

607
00:39:49,256 --> 00:39:51,124
Lucky for us, right?

608
00:39:53,227 --> 00:39:54,428
- Grandma.
- Yes?

609
00:39:54,428 --> 00:39:55,929
Let's go eat something delicious.

610
00:39:55,929 --> 00:39:57,664
- Okay, let's go.
- Okay.

611
00:39:58,765 --> 00:40:01,635
So, are you sleeping well these days?

612
00:40:02,569 --> 00:40:04,004
I sleep when I can.

613
00:40:05,339 --> 00:40:06,607
- Grandma.
- Yes?

614
00:40:06,607 --> 00:40:07,975
I had another weird dream.

615
00:40:08,141 --> 00:40:10,310
What? Did you turn into a bear again?

616
00:40:10,310 --> 00:40:11,278
No.

617
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:15,082
In the dream, someone…

618
00:40:15,449 --> 00:40:18,051
grabbed my hand
and was dragging me somewhere.

619
00:40:18,352 --> 00:40:20,387
- What?
- But…

620
00:40:22,856 --> 00:40:24,992
I couldn't find you,
so I thought you weren't here.

621
00:40:25,626 --> 00:40:26,593
Thank goodness.

622
00:40:27,895 --> 00:40:29,463
Is this table okay?

623
00:40:29,463 --> 00:40:32,199
- It's a table right in the middle.
- It's fine.

624
00:40:32,799 --> 00:40:35,469
Have you been well?
Is everything all right?

625
00:40:37,304 --> 00:40:38,272
Yes.

626
00:40:38,639 --> 00:40:41,008
Here are the drinks you ordered.

627
00:40:45,712 --> 00:40:47,781
Please enjoy.

628
00:40:50,184 --> 00:40:51,218
Who is that?

629
00:40:51,552 --> 00:40:53,453
The author of a book I like.

630
00:40:53,887 --> 00:40:56,723
I found her by chance, even though she was
in hiding for so long.

631
00:41:00,127 --> 00:41:02,396
This place is perfect for dates.

632
00:41:02,396 --> 00:41:05,432
The food is great, and the staff is kind.

633
00:41:11,004 --> 00:41:12,406
Here's your appetizer.

634
00:41:12,406 --> 00:41:15,742
It's a soup made with seasonal
parsnips, topped with truffle foam…

635
00:41:15,742 --> 00:41:18,078
and burdock crisps.

636
00:41:18,645 --> 00:41:21,315
Next time, bring Da Hong, not me.

637
00:41:22,549 --> 00:41:25,018
Why would I take Da Hong to a date spot?

638
00:41:25,018 --> 00:41:28,222
Well, should young people
hang out at their houses all the time?

639
00:41:29,523 --> 00:41:31,258
You know we're not like that.

640
00:41:32,326 --> 00:41:34,294
Enjoy your meal.

641
00:41:37,030 --> 00:41:39,600
Chef, I'll come again next time.

642
00:41:39,600 --> 00:41:42,803
We'd be happy to have you,
but come to eat, not to talk shop.

643
00:41:44,404 --> 00:41:45,606
My goodness, no way!

644
00:41:45,606 --> 00:41:46,773
Hello.

645
00:41:47,007 --> 00:41:49,009
My goodness, you too, ma'am?

646
00:41:49,743 --> 00:41:51,612
Did you come to eat with your grandmother?

647
00:41:52,346 --> 00:41:55,949
I'm a writer for the pilot variety show,
"Let's Have a Meal."

648
00:41:55,949 --> 00:41:58,853
I sent the program proposal
to Manager Kim Yeong Su,

649
00:41:58,878 --> 00:42:00,313
and I wondered if you had seen it.

650
00:42:03,090 --> 00:42:06,059
Our show is where stars visit
an ordinary home…

651
00:42:06,059 --> 00:42:08,395
and make a home-cooked meal together.

652
00:42:08,629 --> 00:42:10,364
You know "Rooftop Romance," right?

653
00:42:10,364 --> 00:42:12,533
It's made by the same production company.

654
00:42:12,900 --> 00:42:17,471
As pilot guests, we'd love to have
Tak Mu I and Chef Kang Hee Su.

655
00:42:17,471 --> 00:42:19,306
We want the two of you so badly…

656
00:42:19,306 --> 00:42:21,575
that we're putting in a lot of effort.

657
00:42:21,575 --> 00:42:23,010
Sounds fun.

658
00:42:24,011 --> 00:42:26,880
So you're the man who was photographed
with Mu I?

659
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:28,382
It was you, Chef.

660
00:42:28,682 --> 00:42:30,551
Nice to meet you. I'm Kang Hee Su.

661
00:42:30,551 --> 00:42:32,586
I've only had the appetizer,

662
00:42:32,586 --> 00:42:34,755
but the food is so refined and delicious.

663
00:42:34,755 --> 00:42:37,324
- Totally my kind of food.
- Thank you.

664
00:42:38,192 --> 00:42:39,526
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

665
00:42:39,526 --> 00:42:41,094
We're in the middle of a meal.

666
00:42:41,161 --> 00:42:42,930
Mu I, do it.

667
00:42:42,930 --> 00:42:44,998
Do it. Try anything and everything.

668
00:42:44,998 --> 00:42:46,700
It's all experience, isn't it?

669
00:42:46,967 --> 00:42:48,702
You're good at cooking.

670
00:42:48,769 --> 00:42:50,804
Thank you, Ma'am!

671
00:42:51,839 --> 00:42:53,507
A variety show? Come on.

672
00:42:53,807 --> 00:42:55,709
Chef would never do it either.

673
00:42:56,677 --> 00:42:57,678
I'll do it.

674
00:43:00,881 --> 00:43:04,484
If Tak Mu I says okay, I'll do it too.

675
00:43:12,659 --> 00:43:15,395
How could I say no when CEO Joo's
company is producing it?

676
00:43:15,495 --> 00:43:17,631
It's all to make our show a success.

677
00:43:17,631 --> 00:43:18,999
Do it with a smile.

678
00:43:21,034 --> 00:43:24,605
Let me be clear. I'm only doing the pilot.

679
00:43:24,838 --> 00:43:27,274
Okay, okay.

680
00:43:27,474 --> 00:43:28,842
Smile.

681
00:43:35,115 --> 00:43:37,584
Hello, sir! Yes.

682
00:43:40,020 --> 00:43:42,556
But why does it have to
be this neighborhood?

683
00:43:43,290 --> 00:43:44,706
It makes me think of her even more.

684
00:43:50,831 --> 00:43:51,999
Are you home?

685
00:43:52,466 --> 00:43:55,435
I'm in your neighborhood today
to shoot a variety show.

686
00:43:58,338 --> 00:43:59,506
You're early.

687
00:43:59,873 --> 00:44:02,342
Well, that's professionalism.

688
00:44:03,677 --> 00:44:05,145
But I'm curious.

689
00:44:05,145 --> 00:44:07,147
You said you hate to be on camera.

690
00:44:07,147 --> 00:44:08,715
So why did you agree to this?

691
00:44:09,082 --> 00:44:10,384
Why else?

692
00:44:11,418 --> 00:44:13,253
Because I want to do this with you, babe.

693
00:44:13,487 --> 00:44:15,989
Could you please
stop saying babe?

694
00:44:16,156 --> 00:44:18,559
At this point, it's become a habit.

695
00:44:19,226 --> 00:44:20,260
Sorry, babe.

696
00:44:23,130 --> 00:44:26,466
Mr. Professional,
I leave myself in your hands.

697
00:44:27,501 --> 00:44:29,136
It's my first variety show appearance too.

698
00:44:29,937 --> 00:44:31,138
By the way,

699
00:44:32,272 --> 00:44:34,441
aren't we rivals today?

700
00:44:35,609 --> 00:44:36,677
Only for today?

701
00:44:37,611 --> 00:44:40,981
- The hosts have arrived!
- Okay.

702
00:44:52,526 --> 00:44:54,428
Unfortunately, we're on the same team.

703
00:44:55,462 --> 00:44:57,297
You don't like me much, Mu I.

704
00:44:58,665 --> 00:45:00,500
Hey, when did I say that?

705
00:45:01,602 --> 00:45:03,837
You have to be honest on variety shows
these days.

706
00:45:06,206 --> 00:45:08,509
Anyway, I want this to become
a regular show…

707
00:45:08,509 --> 00:45:10,611
so I can see Joo Da Hong get jealous.

708
00:45:10,811 --> 00:45:12,946
So work with me today, okay?

709
00:45:13,647 --> 00:45:16,083
I'm going to beat that team today,
no matter what.

710
00:45:18,185 --> 00:45:20,821
Ma'am, which way did the other team go?

711
00:45:21,588 --> 00:45:24,291
- I'm sorry. We'll do it next time.
- No, it's fine.

712
00:45:24,291 --> 00:45:26,627
- Take care.
- Have a good evening.

713
00:45:27,394 --> 00:45:29,263
What a shame.

714
00:45:30,063 --> 00:45:31,999
We can always find someone else anyway.

715
00:45:31,999 --> 00:45:34,134
Shall we go find another meal partner?

716
00:45:34,234 --> 00:45:37,271
I expected it, but this really isn't easy.

717
00:45:37,271 --> 00:45:38,372
No, it isn't.

718
00:45:38,372 --> 00:45:40,374
So once you make eye contact,

719
00:45:40,374 --> 00:45:43,143
lock on like a crocodile and never let go.

720
00:45:43,744 --> 00:45:45,179
- Let's go.
- Okay.

721
00:45:47,514 --> 00:45:48,515
What?

722
00:45:52,653 --> 00:45:53,687
Someone you know?

723
00:45:53,687 --> 00:45:55,856
She's our employee.

724
00:45:56,290 --> 00:45:58,225
- An employee from The Kitchen?
- Yes.

725
00:45:58,559 --> 00:46:01,595
- May I say hello for a moment?
- Sure.

726
00:46:02,029 --> 00:46:03,096
Yu Il.

727
00:46:04,731 --> 00:46:07,501
Chef, you look like a celebrity.

728
00:46:08,836 --> 00:46:10,304
It's so awkward.

729
00:46:10,737 --> 00:46:14,441
But weren't you filming together
with Tak Mu I?

730
00:46:14,842 --> 00:46:17,611
We split up because we're competing.

731
00:46:19,446 --> 00:46:22,649
Which of us will you cheer for?

732
00:46:23,050 --> 00:46:24,184
Who would I cheer for?

733
00:46:27,004 --> 00:46:27,997
Wait a minute.

734
00:46:28,277 --> 00:46:30,357
Why would you hesitate
with your employer right here?

735
00:46:30,657 --> 00:46:32,626
Are you a fan of Tak Mu I?

736
00:46:32,993 --> 00:46:33,961
What?

737
00:46:34,895 --> 00:46:37,331
Hello, I'm comedian Kim Jun Ho.

738
00:46:38,065 --> 00:46:39,099
Your name?

739
00:46:39,099 --> 00:46:40,467
I'm Gong Yu Il.

740
00:46:40,667 --> 00:46:41,635
Gong "Hyu" Il?

741
00:46:41,802 --> 00:46:43,437
No, it's Yu Il.

742
00:46:43,504 --> 00:46:45,706
Not "Hyu Il" but "Yu Il,"
as "the only one."

743
00:46:45,806 --> 00:46:47,274
Only one!

744
00:46:47,274 --> 00:46:50,277
In a way, you're
our only hope right now.

745
00:46:50,277 --> 00:46:51,845
Where are you headed?

746
00:46:52,112 --> 00:46:53,146
I'm going home…

747
00:46:53,280 --> 00:46:54,414
That's perfect!

748
00:46:54,481 --> 00:46:58,852
Then come have a meal with us!

749
00:47:00,654 --> 00:47:02,990
- Wait, this is a bit much…
- What? Why?

750
00:47:03,223 --> 00:47:04,324
No, we…

751
00:47:05,359 --> 00:47:07,928
we don't have the luxury of being picky
about who we choose,

752
00:47:07,928 --> 00:47:09,196
and we have cameras.

753
00:47:09,196 --> 00:47:11,932
Chef, picture yourself preparing a meal…

754
00:47:11,932 --> 00:47:13,534
for your employee.

755
00:47:13,534 --> 00:47:16,370
How heartwarming and wonderful
would that be, right?

756
00:47:16,436 --> 00:47:19,506
But people might say it was staged,
and that could cause backlash.

757
00:47:19,506 --> 00:47:22,843
Right, and my place is a rooftop room,
so it's too small.

758
00:47:23,544 --> 00:47:26,446
Also, the kitchen is too small
for Chef to cook in…

759
00:47:27,214 --> 00:47:31,118
It's already a house on another show,
so it may not be a good look.

760
00:47:31,185 --> 00:47:32,786
Another show? Which show?

761
00:47:33,153 --> 00:47:35,289
"Rooftop Romance."

762
00:47:35,489 --> 00:47:37,758
Tak Mu I's "Rooftop Romance?"

763
00:47:39,626 --> 00:47:40,594
Amazing!

764
00:47:40,594 --> 00:47:43,096
The chef's employee we ran into by chance
on the street just now…

765
00:47:43,096 --> 00:47:46,934
is the actual tenant of Tak Mu I's
"Rooftop Romance."

766
00:47:47,100 --> 00:47:49,603
If we let this go, it could
cause controversy, right?

767
00:47:49,603 --> 00:47:52,172
Ma'am, we'll be accused
of having no instinct.

768
00:47:52,172 --> 00:47:53,473
Push for it.

769
00:47:54,341 --> 00:47:56,143
But I still think…

770
00:47:56,143 --> 00:47:58,812
Of course, we want this badly
for many other reasons,

771
00:47:58,812 --> 00:48:00,647
but we can't just barge in.

772
00:48:01,548 --> 00:48:02,749
How about this?

773
00:48:02,749 --> 00:48:04,651
Without clearing it first
with the employer,

774
00:48:04,751 --> 00:48:08,755
you agree on your own, okay, Yu Il?

775
00:48:08,755 --> 00:48:09,890
That's fine, right?

776
00:48:11,425 --> 00:48:14,127
We never force anyone.
If you don't want to, you don't have to.

777
00:48:14,127 --> 00:48:15,796
But we'd keep walking and just wander

778
00:48:15,796 --> 00:48:19,499
from place to place like beggars
with this one-star chef, and that'd be it.

779
00:48:20,801 --> 00:48:22,736
I'm just kidding. Just kidding.

780
00:48:23,670 --> 00:48:25,038
So, Gong Yu Il,

781
00:48:25,038 --> 00:48:27,374
let's have a meal!

782
00:48:29,009 --> 00:48:30,077
Thank you.

783
00:48:30,077 --> 00:48:32,346
- Come next time.
- Okay, take care.

784
00:48:35,749 --> 00:48:38,185
How many rejections were there just now?

785
00:48:38,185 --> 00:48:40,521
Seven, eight?

786
00:48:41,154 --> 00:48:42,289
That was the ninth one.

787
00:48:42,890 --> 00:48:45,726
- Shall we go over there this time?
- Yes!

788
00:48:46,483 --> 00:48:49,062
Well, we meet again here!

789
00:48:49,696 --> 00:48:51,698
It must be fate!

790
00:48:52,232 --> 00:48:53,300
Someone you know?

791
00:48:53,634 --> 00:48:56,170
I filmed a show in this neighborhood.

792
00:48:56,170 --> 00:48:58,005
She's a local I met then…

793
00:48:58,338 --> 00:48:59,840
How perfect.

794
00:49:00,140 --> 00:49:01,408
Hello.

795
00:49:03,210 --> 00:49:04,678
Wait, what was your name?

796
00:49:05,312 --> 00:49:06,613
I saw you on a show,

797
00:49:06,613 --> 00:49:09,550
where you played Joo Da Hong's friend…

798
00:49:09,950 --> 00:49:12,486
It's Min Ye, Kang Min Ye.

799
00:49:14,087 --> 00:49:16,356
Looks like you're filming something?

800
00:49:16,356 --> 00:49:19,193
Ma'am, have you eaten?

801
00:49:19,193 --> 00:49:20,694
No, not yet.

802
00:49:21,328 --> 00:49:22,362
Then…

803
00:49:22,362 --> 00:49:24,198
- Let's have a meal.
- Let's have a meal.

804
00:49:25,032 --> 00:49:26,166
A meal?

805
00:49:26,300 --> 00:49:29,203
Ma'am, we need to go to an ordinary home…

806
00:49:29,203 --> 00:49:31,138
to share a meal together…

807
00:49:32,573 --> 00:49:35,342
I'm so sorry.
I feel so bad for saying this.

808
00:49:35,943 --> 00:49:37,578
I can't do it today…

809
00:49:37,578 --> 00:49:39,146
I have to go to a birthday café.

810
00:49:39,413 --> 00:49:40,981
A "birthday café?"

811
00:49:41,281 --> 00:49:43,717
You don't know what a birthday café is?

812
00:49:44,318 --> 00:49:48,722
Today is the day our Ryu Min debuted.

813
00:49:49,389 --> 00:49:51,391
It's the day he was reborn as a singer,

814
00:49:51,391 --> 00:49:52,893
so as a fan club,

815
00:49:52,893 --> 00:49:56,230
we have to throw a birthday café,
at least.

816
00:49:58,432 --> 00:50:00,267
So you're not a Tak Mu I fan,

817
00:50:00,267 --> 00:50:01,902
but a Ryu Min fan?

818
00:50:02,069 --> 00:50:06,006
Originally I liked Tak Mu I first,

819
00:50:06,031 --> 00:50:08,008
but while I was watching the show,

820
00:50:08,008 --> 00:50:10,744
our Ryu Min was just so cute,

821
00:50:10,744 --> 00:50:13,914
so I kind of became his fan.

822
00:50:15,115 --> 00:50:16,717
But for me,

823
00:50:16,717 --> 00:50:18,852
Tak Mu I is my favorite, my favorite!

824
00:50:18,852 --> 00:50:21,121
Tak Mu I forever!

825
00:50:21,722 --> 00:50:23,790
I'm going to be late.
Come tomorrow instead!

826
00:50:23,790 --> 00:50:26,894
If you come tomorrow, I'll set out
a 12-dish full table spread, okay?

827
00:50:26,894 --> 00:50:29,530
Come tomorrow!
Good luck. Good luck, everyone!

828
00:50:29,530 --> 00:50:31,064
Okay, take care.

829
00:50:33,033 --> 00:50:34,334
That'll be in the preview.

830
00:50:34,334 --> 00:50:36,336
"Tak Mu I Loses a Fan to Ryu Min"

831
00:50:38,772 --> 00:50:41,375
- Shall we keep going?
- Let's go!

832
00:50:47,648 --> 00:50:49,816
This isn't "Rooftop Romance."

833
00:50:49,816 --> 00:50:51,818
It seems as though a new show…

834
00:50:51,818 --> 00:50:54,121
called "Rooftop Kitchen"
is about to start.

835
00:50:54,321 --> 00:50:55,689
You two…

836
00:50:55,689 --> 00:50:58,025
kind of look good together, I must say.

837
00:50:59,960 --> 00:51:02,329
- Can I taste this?
- Sure, try it.

838
00:51:02,329 --> 00:51:05,132
Then I'm about to try the food myself.

839
00:51:05,132 --> 00:51:06,466
- You too, Yu Il.
- Thanks.

840
00:51:06,466 --> 00:51:08,502
I'm taking a big bite.

841
00:51:13,941 --> 00:51:16,476
- How is it?
- The curry is delicious!

842
00:51:18,278 --> 00:51:20,013
- Is it okay? Is it tasty?
- It's so good.

843
00:51:20,013 --> 00:51:21,481
- Like I said, right?
- Yeah.

844
00:51:21,682 --> 00:51:23,517
This is amazing.

845
00:51:23,650 --> 00:51:24,785
Thank goodness.

846
00:51:36,697 --> 00:51:39,166
I picked you because I thought we'd win.

847
00:51:39,967 --> 00:51:43,270
But you lost to a non-celebrity,
and that's not a good look, is it?

848
00:51:45,005 --> 00:51:46,006
I'm sorry.

849
00:51:47,608 --> 00:51:51,178
Min Ye, I'd think you don't normally eat
convenience store food, right?

850
00:51:52,613 --> 00:51:54,803
It's all my fault.

851
00:51:54,827 --> 00:51:56,116
No, it's fine.

852
00:51:56,116 --> 00:51:57,818
I eat really well, you know.

853
00:51:58,986 --> 00:52:00,220
Then you'd know.

854
00:52:00,888 --> 00:52:02,756
How much is this triangle gimbap?

855
00:52:03,690 --> 00:52:05,459
Well, about…

856
00:52:06,226 --> 00:52:07,394
Forty cents?

857
00:52:11,698 --> 00:52:15,169
I've actually tried
everything except that.

858
00:52:15,736 --> 00:52:16,703
Okay.

859
00:52:16,703 --> 00:52:18,272
Eat up. It'll get cold.

860
00:52:24,878 --> 00:52:26,446
It's so delicious.

861
00:52:28,615 --> 00:52:30,784
Cut! We'll stop here.

862
00:52:32,252 --> 00:52:33,453
Good work, everyone.

863
00:52:40,594 --> 00:52:42,129
- Mu I.
- Yes?

864
00:52:42,162 --> 00:52:45,566
The house Chef Kang scouted
is apparently Yu Il's house.

865
00:52:45,566 --> 00:52:46,567
What?

866
00:52:54,441 --> 00:52:57,244
In a little while, we'll shoot
a quick closing and wrap up.

867
00:52:57,244 --> 00:52:58,478
- Okay.
- Okay.

868
00:52:58,478 --> 00:53:00,414
We'll start when Jun Ho arrives.

869
00:53:05,052 --> 00:53:06,119
What did you eat?

870
00:53:07,421 --> 00:53:09,156
Convenience store food, the usual.

871
00:53:09,923 --> 00:53:10,958
Ramyeon?

872
00:53:12,693 --> 00:53:13,827
I heard.

873
00:53:14,061 --> 00:53:15,829
I heard you filmed at Yu Il's place.

874
00:53:16,964 --> 00:53:18,699
Did Yu Il do well without getting nervous?

875
00:53:20,067 --> 00:53:21,235
I was with her.

876
00:53:22,302 --> 00:53:23,437
Exactly.

877
00:53:24,037 --> 00:53:27,441
With a difficult employer
and the unfamiliar cameras,

878
00:53:27,441 --> 00:53:28,842
she must have been flustered.

879
00:53:30,844 --> 00:53:34,515
Looks like you're curious about it,
go check it out on the broadcast.

880
00:53:41,722 --> 00:53:43,257
Thank you for your hard work today.

881
00:53:43,257 --> 00:53:44,625
- Good work.
- Thank you.

882
00:53:44,625 --> 00:53:45,626
Thank you.

883
00:53:45,626 --> 00:53:47,361
- Good work.
- You too. Thank you.

884
00:53:52,533 --> 00:53:55,169
- Yeong Su, go ahead without me.
- Where are you going?

885
00:53:55,836 --> 00:53:57,704
I need to see Kkong.

886
00:53:57,804 --> 00:54:00,207
No, you'd be a nuisance at this hour.

887
00:54:00,207 --> 00:54:01,575
Well, why not?

888
00:54:01,575 --> 00:54:03,410
I want to eat with Kkong too!

889
00:54:03,410 --> 00:54:05,078
What, another meal?

890
00:54:08,048 --> 00:54:09,950
Fine, I'll take you, but I'm coming along.

891
00:54:09,950 --> 00:54:10,918
Really?

892
00:54:10,918 --> 00:54:14,221
But I'm going to wait downstairs.
Just one hour.

893
00:54:14,221 --> 00:54:16,523
- You come down after just one hour, okay?
- Okay.

894
00:54:16,523 --> 00:54:17,624
Get in.

895
00:54:24,364 --> 00:54:27,768
The person you are trying
to reach is not available.

896
00:54:27,768 --> 00:54:29,736
Please try again later.

897
00:54:32,472 --> 00:54:34,107
I'll get you a new spoon.

898
00:54:35,209 --> 00:54:37,177
You were doing that with a straw before.

899
00:54:37,177 --> 00:54:39,213
This is technically equivalent
to kissing...

900
00:54:41,014 --> 00:54:42,349
But…

901
00:54:43,250 --> 00:54:46,019
if you're going to,
might as well be on the lips…

902
00:54:46,286 --> 00:54:49,456
Chef, I think you've just crossed
the line…

903
00:54:50,591 --> 00:54:53,827
I'd like to cross the line
just for a moment.

904
00:55:12,546 --> 00:55:14,581
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
